 in the highly desirable ""Montecillo"" neighborhood is a rare find. Situated in a peaceful cul-de-sac, this wonderful home offers a great floor plan. Upon entering, you are greeted by a formal living room with onyx fireplace and an adjoining formal dining room. The open kitchen boasts spacious granite countertops, stainless steel appliances and a walk-in pantry. Two spacious bedrooms are adjoined by a Jack and Jill bathroom that opens to the pool. Another bedroom features an updated ensuite bathroom with a shower. The bright and open primary bedroom features a seating area, a walk-in closet, and a large, updated walk-in shower with dual sinks. Recessed light and dual pane windows throughout. The expansive flat backyard includes a pool, a built-in BBQ, a fire pit, fountain and multiple seating areas/bars, offering ample space for play, entertaining or enjoying your own private oasis. A private fenced patio off the living room can be transformed into a kid's playground, garden, or anything you desire. The house offers significant potential with its large yard, including the possibility for an ADU. The long driveway is a bonus. The neighborhood is characterized by wide tree-lined streets and is close to award-winning Palos Verdes Unified School District schools. It also offers many equestrian riding rinks for horseback riding, the Rolling Hills Country Club for golfing, and the Jack Kramer Club for tennis or swimming. This is a rare opportunity to own a true gem in one of the most sought-after neighborhoods in the Palos Verdes Peninsula.","","Entry, Family Room, Jack & Jill, Kitchen, Living Room, Main Floor Bedroom, Main Floor Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite, Walk-In Closet, Walk-In Pantry","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","SWOODHOW","Tiana","Capper","sbcapptia","S5267","2.5","%","Vista Sotheby?s International Realty","2435000","False","Full Service","Text Lauren@310-619-4989 for showing request and CBS Code. Preferred 24 hours notice please.","True","None"