s, Homeowners Association","4700000","All personal artwork and furnishings, five brass antique ceiling fixtures in one hallway area. Primary bedroom fireplace fender.","","4700000","#ERR","310-936-1283","","leslie@bhhscp.com","310-544-3071","Leslie","310-377-7239","","Stetson","","VSTETLES","","","310-265-2177","","V7804","310-544-3071","Berkshire Hathaway HomeService","310-544-5091","","Exclusive Right To Sell","-118.339906","","64","75869","0-1 Unit/Acre, Front Yard, Garden, Gentle Sloping, Horse Property, Horse Property Unimproved, Landscaped, Lawn, Lot Over 40000 Sqft, Rectangular Lot, Sprinkler System, Sprinklers Drip System, Sprinklers In Front, Sprinklers In Rear, Sprinklers Timer","Hiking , Gutters, Horse Trails, Rural","Gated with Attendant, Carbon Monoxide Detector(s), Smoke Detector(s)","Assessor","","","PV24193335","0","3","3","2","1","Owner","","","","Guest House, Guest House Detached","Driveway, Paved, Driveway Up Slope From Street, Garage, Garage Faces Side, Garage - Three Door, Garage Door Opener, Gated, Guest, On Site","True","Patio, Patio Open, Front Porch, Stone","True","1","","None","False","Negotiable","1161.93","Stunning Turnkey Home in the City of Rolling Hills! This estate-like home was upgraded in recent years. These upgrades include things like high quality woods for all new cabinets, moldings, passage doors, paneling, hardwood floors and fencing. Other features include new Marvin windows and doors, a new ceramic wood look tile roof, new pavered driveway/patios and new stonework. Additionally, there are all new bathroom fixtures and electrical work which includes state of the art Lutron Systems and top of the line LED lighting. Situated on a spacious lot of usable and fenced land, this home also features a detached guest house. With sweeping views of the Santa Monica Bay, The Los Angeles Basin, Downtown LA and Mountain Ranges beyond, this home is private and gated. There is a 426 foot guest house in addition to the 4045 foot main house (total sgft of 4471).The guest house  has a bathroom and features new floors and extensive storage options. The three car garage offer walls of cabinetry as well. As you enter the home, along a stone pathway and covered porch, you enter a tasteful and elegant interior that preserves a classical style. The paneled living room overlooks downtown Los Angeles and flows to the dining room and a charming sitting room with a fireplace. The kitchen and large great room provide an open gathering space with a cathedral beamed ceiling. The kitchen has newer stainless appliances and ""soft touch"" maple cabinetry and a large island connects to a casual dining area. The great room offers a large seating area with lighted display bookshelves and a hidden bar for wine storage. There is direct access to the backyard patio area which is a perfect setting for outside parties and entertaining. The neutral color palette and classic design are accented with rich lighting fixtures and wall sconces. These are just some of the many features of this home. All of the three bathrooms have been redone with new surfaces and fixtures. There are four bedrooms and an office and all of the bedrooms have lovely views. The primary bedroom features a fireplace and comfortable sitting area inside and outside access to a stone patio with spectacular night views. The primary bathroom is beautiful with attention to function and quality ""Ann Sacks"" marble. This equestrian community offers miles of private trails and lighted tennis and pickle ball courts. With access to both the nationally rated Palos Verdes School District and Chadwick School, this home will delight!","Composition, Fire Retardant","All Bedrooms Down, Attic, Den, Entry, Family Room, Formal Entry, Foyer, Great Room, Kitchen, Laundry, Library, Living Room, Main Floor Primary Bedroom, Primary Bathroom, Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite, Office, Walk-In Closet","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","Chris","Adlam","VADLACHR","V8107","","",