 the approximate 20,000 Palos Verdes homes, only a handful command the astonishing, jaw-dropping views encompassing BOTH the Santa Monica Bay AND the Long Beach/Newport Coast.  This home lovingly caressed a family for two generations who not only enjoyed this rare view, but also the orange, grapefruit, avocado and apple trees; t's now time to ""pass the torch"" to the next lucky owner.  All on one level, a true classic Ranch Style home built to take advantage of the astonishing views from nearly every room.  The floor plan flows efficiently with nary any wasted space; the feel is much larger than the 2063 square feet shown in the LA County Tax Records.  Summer evenings will be enjoyed by all around the pool.  There's plenty of additional land to garden, for kids to play, grow your gardens, and be at peace after a long day at work.  Commuters to Long Beach or Downtown Los Angeles/Century City will find this location ideal as the Harbor Fwy on ramp is just a few short minutes away.  And of course the Palos Verdes Schools serving this neighborhood are ranked among the best in the United States.  The home is located at the end of a very private cul-de-sac which enhances safety and the homes sits in a way in which your enjoyment and privacy are maximized.  Yes, the home is dated, and the ""value-pricing"" reflects your opportunity to invest with the potential of massive returns on every dollar; but only if you don't miss out and delay.  Demand for property like this is immense, but you don't need a real estate agent to tell you that ... you've seen enough homes already to know, deep down in your soul, THIS IS YOUR HOME!  It's time to make an offer!  Seller will work with you!","Composition","All Bedrooms Down, Family Room, Living Room, Main Floor Bedroom, Main Floor Primary Bedroom, Primary Bathroom, Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","Dapplegray","Palos Verdes Peninsula","Miraleste","SBSANDJAM","Marta","Jackson","PVJACKMAR","V7186","",""