 like your own private mountain resort. Nestled into an acre of very usable land, the design and layout will impress the most discerning Midmod enthusiasts, while the breathtaking views from the harbor to Catalina will have everyone else amazed. As you open the gorgeous custom front door, you are taken back into a time when architectural design was unique and artistic. The dramatic entry leads to a library with wall-to-wall built-ins and a private nook, as well as the Great Room, featuring cathedral ceilings and floor-to-ceiling windows, and an attached deck that gives you the best of indoor/outdoor living. The dining room enjoys the same panoramic views and connects to the large, refreshed kitchen with quartz countertops, a Zellige Crema tile backsplash, and recessed lighting. The Primary Suite has a newly remodeled bathroom with limestone floors, Isola Capri tile, Kohler fixtures, West Elm hardware, a walk-in shower, and a freestanding tub. There is a spacious walk-in closet and another large closet, making the battles of closet space a thing of the past. The primary bedroom has raised ceilings and French doors that open to another private deck that would be amazing for morning coffee or yoga (or both). On the lower level is a large lounge/den with a fireplace and wet bar that is perfect for when you want more space for your guests. This level has the other three bedrooms and provides an option to open two into one large room. The second bathroom has been completely remodeled with limestone flooring, stunning Zellige Perla tile, Kohler fixtures, and West Elm Hardware to keep the Midmod feel to the house. The exterior is as stunning as the rest of the property, with an expansive flat side yard, large enough to host a wedding (or party of your choice).  As you go down to the pool and spa, your guests can take advantage of the changing room, separate bathroom, and outdoor shower that are perfect for the pool-goers. As you soak in the views and take in the privacy, you may get lost in your original feeling of being at a mountain retreat. However, this mountain retreat is within walking distance to award-winning Mira Catalina Elementary and the new UCLA South Bay campus, and just a short drive to parks, beaches, and nature trails. Not many acre-sized properties come on the market in Los Angeles, and very few have the architectural excellence of this Mid-Century Modern gem.","Shake","Formal Entry, Great Room, Laundry, Library, Living Room, Main Floor Primary Bedroom, Primary Bathroom, Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite, Office, Retreat, Separate Family Room, Utility Room, Walk-In Closet","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","Mira Catalina","","","","Meen ah (Mina)","Hwang","sbhwanmee","sb1350760","","","Compass","3300000","False","Full Service","Please try to come or send clients to open houses. For private appointments, 24 hour notice please; buyer must be pre-approved for list price or higher. Thank you so much.","False","","","True","3707","Assessor","","CA","Closed","Multi/Split ","","","Crest","","3069","Road","","Mid Century Modern","Conventional","","20622","","Single Family Residence","","Cable Available, Electricity Connected, Natural Gas Connected, Phone Available, Sewer Not Available, Water Connected","Catalina, Coastline, Harbor, Ocean, Panoramic","True","https://my.matterport.com/show/?m=EqDPzUG4rM4","https://3069crestrd.com/idx","","1967","90275","6302","RPRS20000*"
