hat is large enough for RV or boat parking. The split level home opens up to hardwood floors that adorn the family room, living room, dining room, kitchen, and ease their way downstairs into the entertainment quarters. The main level of the home enjoys creamy colored walls that are touched by French vanilla cabinetry, granite counters, and gourmet stainless steel appliances from Viking to Frigidaire. The family and dining area are gently brought together by a lovingly large fireplace with wooden mantle, mosaic touches, and a tiled hearth. The downstairs is a great gathering space. Currently designed for an epic game night, the room can be utilized in a wide array of ways. The downstairs enjoys a bathroom, direct access to the finished garage, and linen space. Two sliding French Doors lead to the backyard and the 20,000 sq ft of private lot that accompanies the home. A custom trellis has 2 large fans that produce great air control for those Southern California summer days. A jacuzzi is tremendous for those winter or cooling summer nights. The rising 20k lot is formed in a way to allow immaculate privacy in a serene setting. This allows owners to peacefully melt into the Palos Verdes atmosphere. The upstairs is dedicated to all the living quarters. All four bedrooms are located here, bringing the family together. The primary bedroom further accents this by having room for a proper nursery next to its remodeled master bath. 2 rooms enjoy sweeping ocean views and the third enjoys seamless natural light. All 3 share a wonderfully remodeled bathroom. Situated in Palos Verdes coastal region, and in the heart of its award winning school district makes this a great home for any family to grow its roots in one of the premier Los Angeles locations.","","All Bedrooms Up","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","Clifford","Scherb","SBSCHECLI","S5267","","","Vista Sotheby?s International Realty","1650000","False","Entry Only","Text Jared Yutronich with showing information