his home is ready to welcome its next chapter. Perched above street level, it showcases a Mid-Century Modern meets Ranch-style vibe, complemented by drought-tolerant landscaping and a welcoming covered front porch. Step inside through the impressive double-door entry and into a foyer with original terrazzo marble flooring. To the left, the light-filled living room features a fireplace and oversized windows framing serene views of the Pacific Ocean and Catalina Island. At the heart of the home is a vintage kitchen with generous cabinetry and a breakfast bar that opens to the informal living area?complete with another fireplace, built-in cabinetry, a cozy dining space, natural wood bay window, and swinging French door to access to the lush backyard. A separate laundry room with built-ins adds extra convenience. Tucked at the rear of the home, the primary suite offers privacy, a walk-in closet, dressing area, en-suite ? bath, and sliding glass doors to the backyard. Down the hall, you?ll find three additional bedrooms?two with ocean views?and an updated full bathroom. Storage is plentiful throughout. Recent upgrades include fresh interior paint, plush carpet, new vinyl flooring, modern light fixtures, and updated door hardware. The spacious backyard features mature fruit trees, a grassy lawn, and a patio perfect for entertaining. A two-car garage offers direct access to the home, and the north side of the property has space with potential for RV parking. Ideally located just blocks from scenic ocean bluffs, trails, and Trump National Golf Club. This home also falls within the award-winning Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified School District. A rare opportunity to own a well-loved home in a quiet coastal enclave. Be the second owner of this timeless treasure?don?t wait.","Composition, Shingle","Family Room, Kitchen, Laundry, Living Room, Primary Suite, See Remarks","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","Nicole","Pletkovich","PVPLETNIC","v8460","","","Keller William