an. There is also a side yard dog run. Large front yard with mature palm trees provides a sense of a tropical vacation retreat. 2 car garage and large front parking pad with a paver driveway. Updated kitchen, bathrooms and floors with wide plank white oak floors. This stretch of Rancho Palos Verdes is considered to have the best weather on the Peninsula. There is opportunity for expansion with preliminary plans drawn up. The Abalone Cove tract was one of the first developments in Palos Verdes and provides residents with a private gate and pathway to the Abalone Cove Shoreline Park. The park includes three different sea caves, tide pools full of sea urchins, sea anemones and starfish along with seal and dolphins sitings. Walking distance to Terranea Resort and many hiking trails. Buyer and Buyer's Agent to verify all information.","","Kitchen","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","John","Corrales","SCORRJOH","SB1350760","2.5","%","Compass","1750000","False","Full Service","Please call  Tiana Bisignano-Capper 310-503-2377 for showings","","","","","1823","Estimated","","CA","Closed","One","","","Packet","","26","Road","","","Cash to New Loan","","14649","","Single Family Residence","","","Peek-A-Boo","True","","","","1954","90275","5828","RPRS10000SP*"
