uiet cul-de-sac across from the Portuguese Bend Beach with nearby access to hiking/biking trails, rugged coves, classic surf spots, beaches, and golf. This gorgeous, remodeled home is nestled on a 17,775 square foot lot. The gourmet kitchen is designed for people who like to cook and entertain at the same time. The remodeled kitchen highlights quartzite counters, wine fridge, oversized GE Monogram refrigerator with icemaker, Thermador 6 burner gas cooktop and oven, dishwasher and microwave. Sun streams through the large kitchen skylight window which can be opened for additional ventilation. Adjacent to the kitchen is a convenient laundry room with stackable washer and dryer, utility sink, and extra storage. The kitchen is merged to a spacious dining room by an elegant quartzite peninsula counter/bar large enough for additional seating. The kitchen, dining area and living room overlook the pool with its streaming fountain. Natural light floods through the sliding glass doors on both ends of the vaulted living room ceiling. The light combined with natural light wood floors makes the room bright and cheery. The sizable master ensuite with the bathroom marble tile and quartzite countertop, custom built cabinet, along with the walk-in shower, make for a comfortable and elegant bedroom environment. This room also has plenty of natural light coming from the sliding glass door and windows. The large walk-in closet with built-in drawers and cabinets allow for plenty of room for clothes and accessories. Additional features include motorized sky lights, 220 volt 60amp installed in the garage ready for AV charging, enclosed exterior workspace great for the hobbyist or perfect for additional party prepping area, and you have no rear neighbors. The backyard is designed for entertaining with a resort feeling. Family and friends will enjoy using the large heated pool, spa, and sports court. A large viewing deck allows for amazing views of the ocean and Catalina Island. Spend quiet, cool mornings outside and enjoy the bird songs and the surrounding greenery in the privacy of the backyard. In the evenings, watch the beautiful winter and summer sunsets from the front porch or through the kitchen window. The Seaview neighborhood is a great place to live and its micro-climate based on its unique coastal location offers the best weather on the peninsula.","Composition","Entry, Kitchen, Laundry, Main Floor Primary Bedroom, Primary Bathroom, Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","Mira Catalina","Palos Verdes Peninsula","","","Scarlett","Park","RSPARKSCA","RPAD","2.5","%","Paradise Realty","2262000","False","Full Service","Tax records show 1757 sq ft  The seller enlarged the master suite which now makes the home larger.","","Private, Heated, In Ground","True","True","1860","Seller","","CA","Closed","One","","","Avenger","","32202","Place","","Mid Century Modern","Contract","","22835","","Single Family Residence","","","Canyon, Neighborhood, Ocean","True","https://www.zillow.com/view-3d-home/49207f37-5213-4169-91da-80feec1d9fe1?setAttribution=mls&wl=true","https://www.zillow.com/view-3d-home/49207f37-5213-4169-91da-80feec1d9fe1?setAttribution=mls&wl=true","Double Pane Windows, Skylight(s)","1960","90275","6004","RPRS13000*"
