with high ceilings and a cozy fireplace flows seamlessly to the backyard through sliding glass doors, creating the perfect space for indoor-outdoor living. The private rear yard is a serene retreat, complete with a grassy play area, mature landscaping, and a spacious patio ideal for al fresco dining while enjoying endless sunsets. The formal dining room provides an elegant setting for gatherings, while the well-designed kitchen blends style and function with rich wood cabinetry, quartz countertops, double oven, warming drawer, 5 burner stainless steel cooktop and a charming garden window. A large stainless-steel double-door refrigerator, recessed lighting, and sliding doors opening directly to the yard make this kitchen both practical and inviting. A separate laundry/mudroom with generous storage adds convenience to everyday living. Upstairs, a versatile bonus room offers the flexibility of a home office, playroom or media space. The primary suite is a sanctuary with vaulted ceilings, a dramatic double-door entry, custom shutters, a huge walk-in closet, and, of course, breathtaking ocean views. The en-suite bath features a granite-topped vanity and an oversized tub-shower combination designed for relaxation. With direct access to a rare three-car garage, this home combines comfort, function, and elegance in a spectacular coastal setting. A true gem in Rancho Palos Verdes, Camino Porvenir captures the essence of Southern California living?where ocean views meet timeless design.","","All Bedrooms Down, Family Room, Primary Suite","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","SWOODHOW","Ingo","Schultz","SBSCHUING","S5267","","","Vista Sotheby?s International Realty","2400000","False","Full Service","Text agent Cari Corbalis for viewing appointments 310-704-4014","True","None","False","","2928","Assessor","","CA","Closed","Two","","","Camino Porvenir","","30435","","","Contemporary","Conventional","","29115","","Single Family Residence","","Electricity Connected, Natura